  "question": {
    "text": "The deflection in moving coil galvanometer falls from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math> divisions to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> division when a shunt of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> is applied. The resistance of galvanometer coil will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>96</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>48</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> represents the current per division though the galvanometer.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0059_3b2095281893.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 93px;\"/></p><p>After applying shunt</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0059_dac2cd8e6100.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 182px;\"/></p><p>Now, if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math> is the galvanometer resistance, from the above figure, it can be written that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>24</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>24</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math></p>"
  }
